The formula approach for this kind of multi-rule merge gets ugly fast. Each column needs a nested FILTER+SORT or array formula referencing every other column's logic, and they're fragile when data has blanks. An Apps Script is meaningfully simpler here, so I'd recommend that route.

## Apps Script: Dedupe & Merge

Go to **Extensions > Apps Script**, paste this, and save. Then run `dedupeAndMerge` from the script editor (or attach it to a button/menu).

```javascript
function dedupeAndMerge() {
  const ss = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet();
  const src = ss.getSheetByName("Clean"); // adjust to your sheet name

  // Columns: A=Timestamp, B=Name, C=Email, D=JoinedBefore(cleaned),
  //          E=Phone(cleaned), F=PreferredPark(canonical)
  // Adjust these indices (0-based) if your cleaned columns are elsewhere
  const COL = { ts: 0, name: 1, email: 2, joined: 3, phone: 4, park: 5 };

  const data = src.getDataRange().getValues();
  const headers = data[0];
  const rows = data.slice(1);

  // Group rows by lowercase email (skip blank emails — they stay as-is)
  const groups = {};
  const noEmail = [];

  rows.forEach(row => {
    const email = String(row[COL.email]).trim().toLowerCase();
    if (!email) {
      noEmail.push(row);
      return;
    }
    if (!groups[email]) groups[email] = [];
    groups[email].push(row);
  });

  const merged = [];

  for (const email in groups) {
    const g = groups[email];

    // 1. Most recent timestamp
    let bestTs = null;
    g.forEach(r => {
      const t = r[COL.ts];
      if (t instanceof Date && (!bestTs || t > bestTs)) bestTs = t;
    });

    // 2. Longest non-empty name
    let bestName = "";
    g.forEach(r => {
      const n = String(r[COL.name]).trim();
      if (n.length > bestName.length) bestName = n;
    });

    // 3. Latest non-empty phone (by timestamp)
    let bestPhone = "";
    let bestPhoneTs = null;
    g.forEach(r => {
      const p = String(r[COL.phone]).trim();
      const t = r[COL.ts];
      if (p && p !== "REVIEW") {
        if (!bestPhoneTs || (t instanceof Date && t > bestPhoneTs)) {
          bestPhone = p;
          bestPhoneTs = t;
        }
      }
    });

    // 4. JoinedBefore: Yes if ANY row says Yes
    let joined = "No";
    g.forEach(r => {
      if (String(r[COL.joined]).trim() === "Yes") joined = "Yes";
    });

    // 5. Canonical park: most recent non-empty, non-REVIEW value
    let bestPark = "";
    let bestParkTs = null;
    g.forEach(r => {
      const pk = String(r[COL.park]).trim();
      const t = r[COL.ts];
      if (pk && pk !== "REVIEW") {
        if (!bestParkTs || (t instanceof Date && t > bestParkTs)) {
          bestPark = pk;
          bestParkTs = t;
        }
      }
    });

    merged.push([bestTs, bestName, email, joined, bestPhone, bestPark]);
  }

  // Add rows with no email (can't dedupe these automatically)
  noEmail.forEach(r => {
    merged.push([
      r[COL.ts],
      String(r[COL.name]).trim(),
      "",
      String(r[COL.joined]).trim(),
      String(r[COL.phone]).trim(),
      String(r[COL.park]).trim()
    ]);
  });

  // Sort by name
  merged.sort((a, b) => String(a[1]).localeCompare(String(b[1])));

  // Write to a new sheet
  let out = ss.getSheetByName("Merged");
  if (out) out.clear();
  else out = ss.insertSheet("Merged");

  out.appendRow(["Timestamp", "Name", "Email", "JoinedBefore", "Phone", "PreferredPark"]);
  if (merged.length) {
    out.getRange(2, 1, merged.length, 6).setValues(merged);
  }

  // Format
  out.getRange(2, 1, Math.max(merged.length, 1), 1)
     .setNumberFormat("m/d/yyyy hh:mm");
  out.getRange(2, 5, Math.max(merged.length, 1), 1)
     .setNumberFormat("@"); // plain text for phones

  SpreadsheetApp.getUi().alert(
    "Done: " + merged.length + " merged rows written to 'Merged' sheet.\n" +
    noEmail.length + " rows had no email and were kept as-is."
  );
}
```

**What to adjust before running:**

The sheet name on line 3 — change `"Clean"` to whatever your cleaned data sheet is called. The column indices in the `COL` object — if your cleaned columns aren't A through F, update the zero-based indices to match. For example, if your cleaned Yes/No is in column G (the 7th column), set `joined: 6`.

**What it does with your sample data:**

Maya's two rows collapse into one: timestamp `04/03/2021 09:12`, name `Maya Singh` (longest), email `maya@example.com`, JoinedBefore `Yes` (row 1 said y → Yes), phone `5551234` (latest non-empty), park `West Side`. Tom and Rivera pass through as single-row entries. Any row with a blank email lands in the output un-merged, with a count in the alert so you know to review those manually.

**After running,** scan the Merged sheet for blank Phone or Park cells — those are cases where every submission for that person had a REVIEW value, meaning the source data needs manual correction.

```javascript
/* ============================================================
   VOLUNTEER SURVEY — DEDUPE & MERGE (v2)
   Extensions > Apps Script  →  paste  →  save  →  run dedupeAndMerge
   ============================================================ */

// ── CONFIGURATION ──────────────────────────────────────────────
const CONFIG = {
  sourceSheet:      "Clean",   // name of the sheet with cleaned data
  headerRow:        1,         // 1-based row number where headers live
  defaultAreaCode:  "555",     // prepended to 7-digit phone numbers

  // Header names the script will search for (case-insensitive).
  // Change these if your headers are worded differently.
  headers: {
    timestamp: "Timestamp",
    name:      "Name",
    email:     "Email",
    joined:    "JoinedBefore",
    phone:     "Phone",
    park:      "PreferredPark",
  },

  outputMerged: "Merged",
  outputReview: "Review",
};
// ── END CONFIGURATION ──────────────────────────────────────────


function dedupeAndMerge() {
  const ss  = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet();
  const src = ss.getSheetByName(CONFIG.sourceSheet);
  if (!src) {
    SpreadsheetApp.getUi().alert(
      'Source sheet "' + CONFIG.sourceSheet + '" not found.');
    return;
  }

  const data    = src.getDataRange().getValues();
  const headers = data[CONFIG.headerRow - 1].map(h => String(h).trim());

  // ── Resolve column indices from header names ────────────────
  const col = {};
  for (const key in CONFIG.headers) {
    const target = CONFIG.headers[key].toLowerCase();
    const idx = headers.findIndex(h => h.toLowerCase() === target);
    if (idx === -1) {
      SpreadsheetApp.getUi().alert(
        'Header "' + CONFIG.headers[key] + '" not found in row '
        + CONFIG.headerRow + '.\nFound: ' + headers.join(", "));
      return;
    }
    col[key] = idx;
  }

  const rows = data.slice(CONFIG.headerRow); // everything below headers

  // ── Helper: normalise a single phone value ──────────────────
  function normalizePhone(raw) {
    const digits = String(raw).replace(/\D/g, "");
    if (digits.length === 10) return digits;
    if (digits.length === 11 && digits[0] === "1") return digits.slice(1);
    if (digits.length === 7)  return CONFIG.defaultAreaCode + digits;
    return "";  // un-normalisable → will route to Review
  }

  // ── Helper: parse a cell as Date (returns null if invalid) ──
  function parseTs(v) {
    if (v instanceof Date && !isNaN(v)) return v;
    const d = new Date(v);
    return isNaN(d) ? null : d;
  }

  // ── First pass: build enriched row objects ──────────────────
  const enriched = rows.map((r, i) => {
    const phoneCleaned = normalizePhone(r[col.phone]);
    const ts           = parseTs(r[col.timestamp]);
    const nameTrimmed  = String(r[col.name]).trim();
    const emailLower   = String(r[col.email]).trim().toLowerCase();
    const joinedRaw    = String(r[col.joined]).trim();
    const parkRaw      = String(r[col.park]).trim();

    // Determine which fields still need review
    const issues = [];
    if (!ts)                                       issues.push("timestamp");
    if (!phoneCleaned)                             issues.push("phone");
    if (parkRaw === "" || parkRaw === "REVIEW")    issues.push("park");
    if (joinedRaw === "REVIEW")                    issues.push("joined");

    return {
      srcRow:   i + CONFIG.headerRow + 1,  // 1-based sheet row for reference
      ts,
      name:     nameTrimmed,
      email:    emailLower,
      joined:   joinedRaw,
      phone:    phoneCleaned,
      phoneFail: !phoneCleaned,
      park:     parkRaw,
      issues,
      raw:      r,
    };
  });

  // ── Group rows ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  //  Priority 1: group by email (if non-blank).
  //  Priority 2: group remaining rows by normalised name+phone.
  const emailGroups    = {};
  const noEmailRows    = [];

  enriched.forEach(r => {
    if (r.email) {
      if (!emailGroups[r.email]) emailGroups[r.email] = [];
      emailGroups[r.email].push(r);
    } else {
      noEmailRows.push(r);
    }
  });

  // Try to group no-email rows by name+phone
  const namePhoneGroups = {};
  const ungroupable     = [];

  noEmailRows.forEach(r => {
    const nameKey  = r.name.toLowerCase().replace(/\s+/g, " ");
    const phoneKey = r.phone;  // already normalised (or "")
    if (nameKey && phoneKey) {
      const key = nameKey + "|" + phoneKey;
      if (!namePhoneGroups[key]) namePhoneGroups[key] = [];
      namePhoneGroups[key].push(r);
    } else {
      ungroupable.push(r);
    }
  });

  // ── Merge logic (applied to any group of rows) ─────────────
  function mergeGroup(group) {
    // Most recent timestamp
    let bestTs = null;
    group.forEach(r => {
      if (r.ts && (!bestTs || r.ts > bestTs)) bestTs = r.ts;
    });

    // Longest non-empty name
    let bestName = "";
    group.forEach(r => {
      if (r.name.length > bestName.length) bestName = r.name;
    });

    // Email: first non-empty (groups share the same email normally)
    let bestEmail = "";
    group.forEach(r => { if (r.email && !bestEmail) bestEmail = r.email; });

    // JoinedBefore: Yes if any says Yes
    let joined = "No";
    group.forEach(r => {
      if (r.joined === "Yes") joined = "Yes";
    });

    // Latest non-empty, non-failed phone by timestamp
    let bestPhone   = "";
    let bestPhoneTs = null;
    group.forEach(r => {
      if (r.phone) {
        if (!bestPhoneTs || (r.ts && r.ts > bestPhoneTs)) {
          bestPhone   = r.phone;
          bestPhoneTs = r.ts;
        }
      }
    });

    // Most recent non-REVIEW park
    let bestPark   = "";
    let bestParkTs = null;
    group.forEach(r => {
      if (r.park && r.park !== "REVIEW") {
        if (!bestParkTs || (r.ts && r.ts > bestParkTs)) {
          bestPark   = r.park;
          bestParkTs = r.ts;
        }
      }
    });

    // Collect remaining issues on the *merged* result
    const issues = [];
    if (!bestTs)                             issues.push("timestamp");
    if (!bestPhone)                          issues.push("phone");
    if (!bestPark || bestPark === "REVIEW")  issues.push("park");
    if (joined === "REVIEW")                 issues.push("joined");

    return {
      row:    [bestTs, bestName, bestEmail, joined, bestPhone, bestPark],
      issues,
      srcRows: group.map(r => r.srcRow),
    };
  }

  // ── Run merge on every group ────────────────────────────────
  const mergedResults = [];
  const reviewResults = [];
  let   namePhoneGroupedCount = 0;

  function routeResult(result) {
    if (result.issues.length > 0) {
      reviewResults.push(result);
    } else {
      mergedResults.push(result);
    }
  }

  for (const key in emailGroups) {
    routeResult(mergeGroup(emailGroups[key]));
  }

  for (const key in namePhoneGroups) {
    const g = namePhoneGroups[key];
    if (g.length > 1) namePhoneGroupedCount += g.length;
    routeResult(mergeGroup(g));
  }

  // Ungroupable rows go through merge (single-row group) for
  // consistent formatting, then route by issues.
  ungroupable.forEach(r => routeResult(mergeGroup([r])));

  // ── Sort both lists by name ─────────────────────────────────
  const byName = (a, b) => String(a.row[1]).localeCompare(String(b.row[1]));
  mergedResults.sort(byName);
  reviewResults.sort(byName);

  // ── Write output sheets ─────────────────────────────────────
  const outHeaders = [
    "Timestamp", "Name", "Email", "JoinedBefore",
    "Phone", "PreferredPark", "Issues", "SourceRows"
  ];

  function writeSheet(name, results, includeIssues) {
    let sheet = ss.getSheetByName(name);
    if (sheet) {
      sheet.clear();
    } else {
      sheet = ss.insertSheet(name);
    }

    const hdr = includeIssues ? outHeaders : outHeaders.slice(0, 6);
    sheet.appendRow(hdr);

    if (results.length === 0) return sheet;

    const output = results.map(r => {
      const base = r.row.slice();
      if (includeIssues) {
        base.push(r.issues.join(", "));
        base.push(r.srcRows.join(", "));
      }
      return base;
    });

    sheet.getRange(2, 1, output.length, output[0].length).setValues(output);

    // Formatting
    sheet.getRange(2, 1, output.length, 1).setNumberFormat("m/d/yyyy hh:mm");
    sheet.getRange(2, 5, output.length, 1).setNumberFormat("@"); // text phones

    sheet.autoResizeColumns(1, hdr.length);
    return sheet;
  }

  writeSheet(CONFIG.outputMerged, mergedResults, false);
  writeSheet(CONFIG.outputReview, reviewResults, true);

  // ── Summary alert ───────────────────────────────────────────
  SpreadsheetApp.getUi().alert(
    "Dedupe & Merge complete\n" +
    "─────────────────────────\n" +
    "Merged (clean):        " + mergedResults.length + " rows\n" +
    "Review (needs fixes):  " + reviewResults.length + " rows\n" +
    "Blank-email rows grouped\n" +
    "  by Name+Phone:       " + namePhoneGroupedCount + " rows collapsed\n" +
    "\nOutput written to "" + CONFIG.outputMerged +
    "" and "" + CONFIG.outputReview + "" sheets."
  );
}
```

A few notes on what changed and why.

**Header-based column lookup.** The script reads row `CONFIG.headerRow`, lower-cases each cell, and matches against the names in `CONFIG.headers`. If a header isn't found it tells you exactly which one is missing and what it did find, so typos are easy to fix.

**Phone normalization with area code.** Every phone value gets stripped to digits. Eleven digits starting with 1 drops the leading 1. Seven digits gets `CONFIG.defaultAreaCode` prepended (set that to whatever area code is correct for your volunteers). Anything else — too few digits, too many, or blank — routes the merged row to the Review sheet with "phone" listed in the Issues column.

**Blank-email grouping.** Rows without an email get a second chance: if two rows share the same normalized name and the same normalized phone, they're merged together. If a row has no email *and* no usable phone or name, it passes through as a single-row group and almost certainly lands in Review.

**Two output sheets.** The Merged sheet has six clean columns with no extra noise. The Review sheet adds an Issues column (e.g., `phone, park`) and a SourceRows column listing the original sheet row numbers so you can trace back to the raw data quickly.

**To run it:** open the script editor, pick `dedupeAndMerge` from the function dropdown, and hit the play button. The first run will ask for authorization to read and write your spreadsheet.

