Three changes from the previous version:

**Config values** are now `headerRow: 2` and `defaultAreaCode: "415"`, so your 7-digit phones will become `415XXXXXXX` and the script reads headers from row 2.

**SourceRows on Merged.** Both output sheets now include a SourceRows column listing the original row numbers that were collapsed into each merged record. On the Merged sheet it's the 7th column; on Review it's the 8th (after Issues).

**Alert string.** The concatenation is broken onto separate lines with `+` operators and the quotes around sheet names use escaped `\"` instead of the curly Unicode quotes that were causing the issue.

```javascript
/* ============================================================
   VOLUNTEER SURVEY — DEDUPE & MERGE (v2.2)
   Extensions > Apps Script  →  paste  →  save  →  run dedupeAndMerge
   ============================================================ */

// ── CONFIGURATION ──────────────────────────────────────────────
const CONFIG = {
  sourceSheet:      "Clean",
  headerRow:        2,
  defaultAreaCode:  "415",

  headers: {
    timestamp: "Timestamp",
    name:      "Name",
